["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A goose flock is a family business with a long memory. Read its moods and you know when to sit still, when to shoot and when to go home.</p></aside><figure class=\"video\"><video controls preload=\"none\" playsinline src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c5/Canada_goose_%28Branta_canadensis%29_family.webm/Canada_goose_%28Branta_canadensis%29_family.webm.480p.vp9.webm\"></video><figcaption>A goose family: parents and young move as one. <span class=\"credit\">Video: Courtney Celley/USFWS, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canada_goose_(Branta_canadensis)_family.webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a>. Needs internet.</span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Flocks are families: pairs plus this year's young <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Families decide together; the gander leads <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>The alarm ladder and the preflight head toss.</li><li>Flight distance and how geese learn hunting pressure.</li><li>Family life, pairing and rank.</li><li>Old birds versus young birds.</li><li>The habits that put them in front of your gun.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Five panels, the goose alarm ladder. 1: feeding, heads down. 2: alert, a few heads up. 3: tall necks, walking off and honking. 4: head tossing, the signal they are about to fly, 80 percent. 5: flush, gone. Tip: at 2 freeze, at 3 do not move at all, at 4 they are leaving: shoot now if in range or let them go.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The alarm ladder: read it from the hide</text><rect x=\"9\" y=\"50\" width=\"72\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8f3e0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"45\" cy=\"70\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"45\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><g transform=\"translate(41 150) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 Q30 -6 34 14 L28 16 Q24 0 12 -2Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"33\" cy=\"18\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M30 16 Q34 22 36 19\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 24 M2 12 L4 24\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><text x=\"45\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feeding</text><rect x=\"87\" y=\"50\" width=\"72\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f5f5dc\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"123\" cy=\"70\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"123\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><g transform=\"translate(119 150) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><text x=\"123\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Alert</text><rect x=\"165\" y=\"50\" width=\"72\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff4e5\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"201\" cy=\"70\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"201\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><g transform=\"translate(197 146) scale(0.62 0.62)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><text x=\"201\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tall necks</text><rect x=\"243\" y=\"50\" width=\"72\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fde3cf\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"279\" cy=\"70\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"279\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><g transform=\"translate(275 150) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><path d=\"M285 112 q8 -8 14 0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M285 120 q8 8 14 0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"279\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Head toss</text><rect x=\"321\" y=\"50\" width=\"72\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fdecea\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"357\" cy=\"70\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"357\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><g transform=\"translate(353 130) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"357\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Flush</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"224\" width=\"360\" height=\"66\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">At 2: freeze. At 3: do not move at all.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">At 4 they are leaving: shoot now if in range,</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">or let them go (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Heads up, then tall necks, then head tosses, then gone <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>At step 2, freeze. At step 4 they are leaving (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the signals in full</summary><ul><li>Head up is the main watch posture. It is not always alarm; some of it is social (75%, Wildfowl journal).</li><li>Tall necks and walking away with honks: rising alarm (Tip, 65%).</li><li>Head tossing is the preflight signal: side to side or up and down shakes with the neck held straight, before the bird flies or walks to a new spot (80%, Raveling 1969; Black and Barrow).</li><li>Ganders recruit their family into the air fastest after starting to head toss (80%, Raveling 1969, Smithsonian summary).</li><li>Ground threat: a gander lowers its head close to the ground and hisses (80%, Audubon).</li><li>In flight, a flock that starts to climb and swing wide has seen something (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a family of geese stands in stubble. The gander tosses his head side to side, twice. Then the whole family lifts off together and flies up and away. Head tossing is the preflight signal, and ganders get the family up fastest, 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The head toss: the family is about to fly</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"210\" width=\"400\" height=\"90\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9c48f\"/><g><g transform=\"translate(120 190) scale(1.5)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><g><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 18 -12;-14 18 -12;10 18 -12;-14 18 -12;10 18 -12;0 18 -12\" dur=\"1.6s\" begin=\"0.5s;2.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(220 196) scale(1.3 1.3)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(300 200) scale(1.0 1.0)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(355 202) scale(0.9 0.9)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.3s\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.3s\"/><g><g transform=\"translate(120 170) scale(1 1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(210 180) scale(0.9 0.9)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(290 185) scale(0.8 0.8)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(350 190) scale(0.75 0.75)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;30 -60\" begin=\"4.3s\" dur=\"2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><text x=\"120\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gander tosses his head</text><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.3s\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Family lifts off together</text></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ganders get the family up fastest (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>The gander tosses, the family lifts. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>See head tosses? The family is about to fly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Shoot only if in range now; never chase them (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to use it</summary><ul><li>Raveling's study followed 77 marked geese from 10 families, 2 pairs and 35 yearlings, and tied preflight movements to family status <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>When you watch a field from the road, head tossing means the flock is about to go. Note where they fly: that is tomorrow's flight line (Tip).</li><li>In a blind, tossing heads on the ground in front of you means your hide or movement has been seen (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two panels. In a park or quiet farm the flush ring around a flock is small: you get close. In a hunted or wild area the ring is large: they flush far. Flight distance changes from place to place, 70 percent. On hunting days tracked geese moved less and flew sooner when a threat came close, 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">How close before they fly? It depends</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"44\" width=\"170\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8f3e0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"210\" y=\"44\" width=\"170\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fdecea\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Park or quiet farm</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunted or wild area</text><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"150\" r=\"30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><circle cx=\"295\" cy=\"140\" r=\"60\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><g transform=\"translate(99 146) rotate(0) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(289 136) rotate(0) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(113 156) rotate(0) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(303 146) rotate(0) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(105 160) rotate(0) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(295 150) rotate(0) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"105\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You get close</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">They flush far</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Flight distance changes place to place (70%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">On hunt days they move less and fly sooner (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>How close you get depends on the place <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>On hunt days, tracked geese moved less and flew sooner when a threat came close <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the studies</summary><ul><li>Belgium: Canada goose flight initiation distance changed with flock size and other birds, and differed by site; most wary in the least visited reserve, least wary in a busy park (70%, Belgian Journal of Zoology, search preview).</li><li>Pennsylvania, 2025: 134 GPS tagged female geese stayed on two hunted Wildlife Management Areas through the season, at least 165 times more likely to be on them than off (80%, Beatty and others, Movement Ecology; Penn State news).</li><li>On hunting days and during hunting hours they took flight less and walked less, but took flight more as a threat got close <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Older work in Illinois: geese went alert at shots even inside a refuge and left places where disturbance kept them from feeding <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>What it means: hunted geese do not leave the area, they get quieter and harder to approach (Tip, 65%).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Pressure sign</th><th>What to change (Tip, 65%)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Birds land 200 m off your spread</td><td>Move to where they landed next time</td></tr><tr><td>Flocks flare at 100 m</td><td>Fix the hide; fewer blinds</td></tr><tr><td>Birds stop using the field</td><td>Rest it a week</td></tr><tr><td>Same flock every hunt</td><td>Change the spread size and shape</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>They avoid fields where they are disturbed again and again <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Same spread, same spot, every day: they learn it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the guide advice</summary><ul><li>Hunting the same spot with the same spread teaches local birds to avoid it. Change decoy count and layout through the season (65%, Ducks Unlimited goose guide).</li><li>Smaller, more realistic spreads in places other hunters do not use <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Fewer blinds: with six hunters, three blinds and rotate shooters <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>\"Rest the field\" is widely repeated hunter advice. No study measured how long (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a goose flock made of five family groups, each circled: two dark birds, the pair, with 1 to 4 brown young. The young stay with their parents a full year, 80 percent. Geese find a mate in their second year and usually pair for life, 80 percent. Most first nest at 2 or 3 years old, 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A flock is a crowd of families</text><ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"95\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><g transform=\"translate(68 87) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(68 103) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(102 87) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(102 103) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(124 87) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><ellipse cx=\"210\" cy=\"85\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><g transform=\"translate(188 77) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(188 93) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(222 77) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(222 93) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"100\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><g transform=\"translate(298 92) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(298 108) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(332 92) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(332 108) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(354 92) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(354 108) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><ellipse cx=\"130\" cy=\"175\" rx=\"45\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><g transform=\"translate(108 167) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(108 183) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(142 167) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><g transform=\"translate(238 162) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(238 178) rotate(0) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(272 162) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(272 178) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(294 162) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dark: pair. Brown: young of the year</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Young stay with parents a full year (80%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mate in 2nd year, usually for life (80%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">First nest at 2 or 3 years old (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Young stay a full year; pairs usually last for life <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Most first nest at 2 or 3 years old <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: families in full</summary><ul><li>A goose finds a mate in its second year and usually stays paired for life; a bird that loses its mate will pair again (80%, Hinterland Who's Who; Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>Fall flocks are families travelling together, from a few families to thousands of birds <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Families with young fly as a unit; you will often see 4 to 8 birds in a tight group inside a big flock (Tip).</li><li>The gander guards the nest and the brood; both parents tend the young (80%, Audubon).</li><li>About half of hatched goslings survive to fly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Shoot the lead bird of a family and the rest often swing back (hunter lore, Tip). Ethics first: take only clean shots.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-geese-stubble.jpg\" alt=\"A winter flock in stubble: old birds and young birds together.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A winter flock in stubble: old birds and young birds together. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Andrea_44 from Leamington, Ontario , Canada, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Geese_in_the_corn_field_stubble_(5372865305).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Young of the year decoy more readily (Tip, widely reported).</li><li>Old birds come in high, circle wide and land short (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Old hand's rule (tradition, opinion)</div><p>Early season and family groups come easy. Late season singles and pairs are the professors. Hunters widely repeat this; no study tested it.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what is fact and what is lore</summary><ul><li>Fact: most geese that survive year one live 10 or more years <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. So many birds in a flock have survived several seasons <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Fact: hunted geese change behaviour on hunt days (80%, Pennsylvania study).</li><li>Lore: old ganders lead the flock away from danger and young birds break off to decoys (Tip).</li><li>Lore: a lone goose that has lost its family is easier to call (Tip).</li><li>Use the lore to choose tactics, not to decide what is legal or ethical.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Six cards, habits geese cannot help. 1: they go back to yesterday&#x27;s field, 65 percent. 2: they land into the wind, 80 percent. 3: they fly late on cold or cloudy mornings, 80 percent. 4: they avoid edges near cover that can hide predators, a Tip. 5: they trust their own kind, a Tip. 6: same roost and same flight line, a Tip. Every habit is a place to wait for them.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6 habits a goose cannot help</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"110\" height=\"115\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"64\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"75\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Back to</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">yesterday&#x27;s field</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(65%)</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"40\" width=\"110\" height=\"115\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"64\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lands into</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the wind</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(80%)</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"40\" width=\"110\" height=\"115\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"325\" cy=\"64\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"325\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Late on cold or</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cloudy mornings</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(80%)</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"165\" width=\"110\" height=\"115\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"189\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"75\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Avoids edges</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">near cover</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Tip)</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"165\" width=\"110\" height=\"115\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"189\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Trusts its</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">own kind</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Tip)</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"165\" width=\"110\" height=\"115\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"325\" cy=\"189\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"325\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same roost,</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">same flight line</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Tip)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Every habit is a place to wait for them</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Every habit is a place to wait for them (Tip).</li><li>Best one: back to yesterday's field <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: each habit and its source</summary><ul><li>In the morning geese usually return to the field they fed in the afternoon before (65%, Ducks Unlimited goose guide; quick lesson).</li><li>They land into the wind, so the wind sets your hide and landing hole (80%, quick lesson; Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>Cold or cloudy mornings: they fly later (80%, Raveling 1972).</li><li>They avoid decoys near fence lines, brush piles and ditches that could hide a predator (60%, Outdoor Life search preview).</li><li>They trust their own kind: decoys work (Tip).</li><li>Same roost and flight line day after day while undisturbed (Tip, 65%). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-06\">Chapter 6</a>.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Memory rhymes (made for this app)</div><ul><li>\"Heads up, sit tight. Necks tall, no fight. Heads toss, take flight.\"</li><li>\"Yesterday's field is tomorrow's yield.\"</li><li>\"Families come easy; the old ones come wary.\"</li></ul></aside><ul><li>Number trick: <strong>2, 2 or 3, 10</strong>. Mate in year 2, first nest at 2 or 3, many live 10 years or more <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Old hand's rule (tradition, opinion)</div><p>Never bump a feeding flock off the field. Let them leave on their own, then hunt them tomorrow. A standard rule in goose scouting guides.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Raveling 1969, Penn State 2025, Belgian flight distance study, Hinterland Who's Who, Audubon, Ducks Unlimited goose guide. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://sora.unm.edu/sites/default/files/journals/auk/v086n04/p0671-p0681.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Raveling 1969, Preflight and flight behavior of Canada geese, Auk 86:671</a>, search preview and <a href=\"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-do-canada-geese-get-ready-to-fly-533259/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Smithsonian summary</a>, 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://psu.edu/news/research/story/despite-knowing-where-and-when-people-hunt-canada-geese-dont-flee-far\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Penn State news on Beatty and others 2025, Movement Ecology</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://belgianjournalofzoology.eu/BJZ/article/download/23/32/53\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Belgian Journal of Zoology, Canada goose flight initiation</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wildfowl.wwt.org.uk/index.php/wildfowl/article/download/833/833\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildfowl journal, Canada goose vigilance</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.hww.ca/en/wildlife/birds/canada-goose.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hinterland Who's Who</a> and <a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/canada-goose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Audubon</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/hunting/goose-hunting-tips-tactics/the-ultimate-guide-to-hunting-canada-geese\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited goose guide</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://outdoorlife.com/blogs/hunting/2013/12/waterfowl-hunting-tip-brush-your-blind-first\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life, brush your blind first</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Full log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-geese.md</code>.</li></ul></details>"]